// ptr -- the pointer, sampled once a frame.
//
// The seam reports pointer *state* rather than pointer events (gfx_mouse_x/y and
// a button bitmask, as of the last poll), so the engine samples it at one known
// instant -- the end of inp_drain, with the event queue empty -- and every
// question during the frame is answered from that snapshot. Nothing in a frame
// can then see the mouse in two places.
//
// The backend speaks *window* pixels and everything above this line speaks
// *surface* pixels, and those are now the same thing: the surface is the window.
// So the map is the identity and all that is left is the clamp.
//
// The clamp is not decoration. The pointer is reported outside the window while a
// drag is in progress -- which is exactly when a game asks where it is -- and an
// unclamped coordinate becomes an out-of-range list index, which aborts.
//
// A game that wants its own units asks for stage coordinates instead
// (sys_sx/sys_sy and sys_vp's scale); those are a different question and the two
// were previously conflated because the surface and the stage were one buffer.
//
// **The button mask must be read exactly once a frame, and this is where.** Its
// three real buttons are state, but its two wheel bits are a *latch*: a wheel
// notch has no duration -- the platform delivers a press and a release together
// -- so the backend sets the bit and the read clears it. A second reader in the
// same frame would see no wheel and the first would still consume it, so there
// is one, here, and every question during the frame is answered from inp_mo.
//
// That latch is why the wheel works at all. Held as ordinary state it was
// invisible: X drains its whole queue in one poll, so the bit was set and
// cleared before any `id` code looked, and the editor's zoom did nothing on
// either mouse button for as long as it existed.

inp_sample() {
  lset((import inp_mo), 3, (import inp_mo)[2]);
  int b = gfx_mouse_buttons();
  inp_sample_tail(b);
} return void;

inp_sample_tail(int b) {
  lset((import inp_mo), 2, b);
  inp_sample_get_xy();
} return void;
